  "id": "shared-attention",
  "term": "shared attention",
  "definition": "Shared attention is a state in which many people focus on the same event or information at the same time, often while also interacting through media. In the source context, this common focus is linked to spikes in activity and attention becoming concentrated on a smaller number of users rather than being spread across many interpersonal exchanges.",
